# Valgrind suppressions for the PoC-002 W0 ABI test.
#
# WebUI loads GTK and WebKit with dlopen() the first time a window property needs them
# (_webui_load_gtk_and_webkit, reached from webui_new_window and webui_set_center even in
# browser mode). The allocations below are made by the constructors of those libraries
# (glib, gobject, gtk, atk, ...) while dlopen runs _dl_init. They are not allocated by
# WebUI or by the bridge and are never freed by anyone. Every frame list below requires
# _dl_init below dlopen below _webui_load_gtk_and_webkit, so a leak allocated by WebUI
# code or by the test itself can never match.

{
   dlopen-gtk-glib-constructor-definite
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible
   ...
   fun:_dl_init
   ...
   fun:dlopen*
   fun:_webui_load_gtk_and_webkit
}

{
   dlopen-gtk-glib-constructor-reachable
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:_dl_init
   ...
   fun:dlopen*
   fun:_webui_load_gtk_and_webkit
}
